  "label": "User projected onto the worker on the left as 'someone' who had too much gas",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the worker on the left (worker_on_left) through the textual material 'someone had too much gas'. The meme uses the 'camp joke structure' to imply that the worker is the subject of the anecdote, creating an analogical mapping where the user identifies with or imagines themselves as 'someone' experiencing the mishap. This projection is indirect but culturally understood through the meme format, where the viewer is invited to imagine themselves in the role of the person described.",
